      "content": "thanks for starting the math—that 1.56 Hz frequency seems to align really well with the actual recorded data spikes from the impact experiments. it's almost too consistent to be a coincidence.\n\ncan you finish the calculation for the rigidity constant (k)? once we have that value, i want to compare it to the known modulus of standard lunar basalt. if the value k you calculate is orders of magnitude higher than what you'd find in natural rock, that's basically the mathematical proof that the shell is an engineered substance rather than just compressed regolith. \n\nshow me the steps to get to that k value.",
